45b3","name":"2025 International Conference on Computing Technologies (ICOCT)","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/icoct64433.2025.11118799","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/icoct64433.2025.11118799","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/icoct64433.2025.11118799","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/icoct64433.2025.11118799","query":"image steganography detection benchmark","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:33:03Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-e0f437c614af087a","title":"Proactive Deepfake Detection via Self-Verifiable Semantic Watermarking","title_zh":"","year":2025,"publication_date":"","abstract":"Malicious Deepfakes pose serious security risks by producing highly realistic forged faces. While numerous countermeasures have been developed to train binary Deepfake classifiers, their limited generalization capacity restricts practical deployment. To proactively defend against Deepfakes, we propose SVS-WM, a Self-Verifiable Semantic Watermarking strategy. The core idea behind SVS-WM is to embed pairs of correlated watermarks within facial semantics, leveraging the inherent fragility of these features, i.e., any semantic modification will disrupt the watermark correlation, thereby enabling robust Deepfake detection. SVS-WM employs a facial semantic disentanglement and reconstruction network, allowing semi-fragile watermarks to be embedded concurrently across multiple semantic levels, including identity and multi-levels of attributes. Specifically, pairs of pseudo-random noise watermarks are adaptively injected into facial attribute and identity features. During propagation stage, the protected image may encounter identity or facial attributes manipulations, we then detect Deepfakes by verifying the correlation result between the decoded attribute watermark and the extracted identity vector. This unique cross-verification mechanism enables authentication without requiring original reference watermark, thereby realizing blind Deepfake detection. Extensive experiments validate the effectiveness of our approach, achieving an average detection accuracy of 98.19% across diverse Deepfake manipulations.","authors":[{"id":"2307632921","name":"Peiqi Jiang","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2267295896","name":"Bohan Lei","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2301539128","name":"Yuhao Sun","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2115715779","name":"Lingyun Yu","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2265575625","name":"Zhineng Chen","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2376105041","name":"Hongtao Xie","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2244112150","name":"Yongdong Zhang","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-acmmm","name":"ACM Multimedia","short_name":"ACM MM","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[{"system":"CCF","level":"A","category":"计算机图形学与多媒体","scope":"","is_top":false,"version":"第七版（2026）","source_url":"https://www.ccf.org.cn/Academic_Evaluation/By_category/","verified_at":"2026-07-16"}]},"task_tags":["content_provenance","deepfake_detection","digital_watermarking"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1145/3746027.3755587","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"2f5c8d2151a23faf3eda15938e72fc21905306b1","primary_url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/2f5c8d2151a23faf3eda15938e72fc21905306b1","citation_count":2,"provenance":[{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"2f5c8d2151a23faf3eda15938e72fc21905306b1","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/2f5c8d2151a23faf3eda15938e72fc21905306b1","query":"facial image manipulation detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T18:32:50Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1145/3746027.3755587","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3746027.3755587","query":"deepfake image detection ACM Multimedia","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:07:06Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-3c4a4d23bb2ab67a","title":"Security Analysis Of Optimized Modern Steganography With The Use Of Encryption, Compression, And Anti-Steganalysis","title_zh":"","year":2025,"publication_date":"","abstract":"This research discusses the development of a modern steganography system based on discrete frequency domain (DCT) adaptation with the integration of adaptive compression and encryption methods to improve the efficiency, robustness, and security of hidden data in digital images. This system is developed in two operating modes, namely append mode and DCT mode. The append mode places the payload at the end of the image file without changing the pixels, so that the Peak Signal-to-Noise Ratio (PSNR) and Root Mean Square Error (RMSE) values are identical to the original image. While the DCT mode inserts data at the mid-frequency AC coefficients adaptively to maintain visual quality and reduce the steganalysis detection footprint. The proposed system supports LZ77/LZ78-based adaptive compression and authenticated AES-256-GCM encryption. Comprehensive testing on 19 cover images shows that the proposed DCT mode achieves a 100% success rate and superior visual quality (average PSNR of 43.97 dB), significantly outperforming the simple DCT method which fails on 42.1% of the test images. These results confirm that the proposed system meets the characteristics of a robust, efficient, and secure steganography system for secret digital communications.","authors":[{"id":"2422381183","name":"Angki","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2422381723","name":"Ady W Paudu","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"71955836","name":"Mukarramah Yusuf","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-f4742dbc7edee5","name":"2025 5th International Conference of Science and Information Technology in Smart Administration (ICSINTESA)","short_name":"","type":"unknown","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/icsintesa68165.2025.11413645","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"062dce4ee840b3a798d2cf131968d82ee97eb161","primary_url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/062dce4ee840b3a798d2cf131968d82ee97eb161","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"062dce4ee840b3a798d2cf131968d82ee97eb161","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/062dce4ee840b3a798d2cf131968d82ee97eb161","query":"image steganalysis detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T18:33:13Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-66382987fa1c2f7a","title":"VGG16Unet: effective passive model for image splicing forgery localization","title_zh":"","year":2023,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-8a13bdcdcf98f6","name":"Shipra Jain","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-cfcc59dceb825e","name":"Durgesh Singh","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-5155795bc8cfe6","name":"Journal of Electronic Imaging","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"1017-9909","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1117/1.jei.32.4.043015","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/1.jei.32.4.043015","citation_count":2,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1117/1.jei.32.4.043015","url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/1.jei.32.4.043015","query":"image forgery localization","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:05:33Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-c2589a34e5c05e7a","title":"An Optimized Fragile Image Watermarking Method for Tamper Detection and Recovery Using SPIHT and Reed-Solomon Coding","title_zh":"","year":2022,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-a5049cd7564203","name":"Mahmoud Alnaanah","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-c62202c5cd5480","name":"Moath Alsafasfeh","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-3e5ddd220957fe","name":"Ahmad Aljaafreh","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-08ef6037ae559d","name":"Amir Aish","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-941ed3ee225b33","name":"Jordan Journal of Electrical Engineering","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"2409-9600","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["digital_watermarking"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.5455/jjee.204-1630865748","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.5455/jjee.204-1630865748","citation_count":1,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.5455/jjee.204-1630865748","url":"https://doi.org/10.5455/jjee.204-1630865748","query":"fragile watermark image tamper localization","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:31:12Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-81ac0847df23257a","title":"Copy-Move Forgery Detection-A Study and the Survey","title_zh":"","year":2022,"publication_date":"2022-08-11","abstract":"The issues caused due to image manipulations are common these days. Furthermore, it causes severe troubles in news broadcasting, social media, and even in digital media forensics. Mainly, the types of image manipulations can be divided into four; they are splice forgery, copy-move, morphing, and retouching. Among these 4 types, copy move forgery is challenging to detect since the image characteristics is not changing even after the forgery. Also, the manipulated images can undergo attacks including rotation, scaling and distortion making it even hard to detect the forgery. In this survey paper, we have reviewed the types of image manipulations and elaborated on copy-move forgery detection and the challenges faced in copy-move forgery detection. The paper has reviewed seminal copy-move forgery-related research articles published between the year 2011-2022.","authors":[{"id":"a5028175779","name":"A. Venugopalan","orcid":"0000-0001-7153-5270","institution_ids":["i81556334"]},{"id":"a5067207797","name":"G. Gopakumar","orcid":"0000-0003-1559-5150","institution_ids":["i81556334"]}],"institution_ids":["i81556334"],"venue":{"id":"venue-9e5fcd3a6db536","name":"2022 Third International Conference on Intelligent Computing Instrumentation and Control Technologies (ICICICT)","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"survey","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/icicict54557.2022.9917647","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W4312852558","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/icicict54557.2022.9917647","citation_count":6,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W4312852558","url":"https://openalex.org/W4312852558","query":"image retouching detection forensics","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T03:56:55Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-fffb2df4d09b837a","title":"Dual image-based reversible fragile watermarking scheme for tamper detection and localization","title_zh":"","year":2022,"publication_date":"2022-12-12","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"a5054697970","name":"Adıtya Kumar Sahu","orcid":"0000-0003-4257-0688","institution_ids":["i81556334"]},{"id":"a5054396197","name":"Monalisa Sahu","orcid":"0000-0002-6928-7017","institution_ids":["i4210139271"]},{"id":"a5008324059","name":"Pramoda Patro","orcid":"0000-0003-3942-3927","institution_ids":["i875944469"]},{"id":"a5012405199","name":"Gupteswar Sahu","orcid":"0000-0002-0263-1346","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5090967969","name":"Soumya Ranjan Nayak","orcid":"0000-0002-4155-884X","institution_ids":["i67357951"]}],"institution_ids":["i4210139271","i67357951","i81556334","i875944469"],"venue":{"id":"venue-d41f806f2dcfa0","name":"Pattern Analysis and Applications","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_